6.2.1  Ways to authenticate work

You must be confident that the work you mark is the
student’s own. Every student must produce their own
work independently under teacher supervision. You
must use enough supervision, or complete sufficient
checks, to be able to judge the authenticity of the
student’s work.

Wherever possible, the teacher should discuss work-in-
progress with students. This will make sure that work
is being completed in a planned and timely way and
provide opportunities for you to check authenticity of
the work.

create or use practice assignments and practice
data which are similar in nature to those set by us

•	 use past OCR-set assignments, or amend past set

