overall aims of the market research’

•	 point out where the work sits within the mark
bands but students must make their own
decisions as to what to improve and how. For
example, the feedback can say ‘this shows a
sound understanding’ (for mark band 2) but not
precisely what should be added to make it show a
comprehensive understanding (for mark band 3).

Feedback must not:

•	 point out specific gaps, for example you must not
prompt the student to include specific detail in
their work, such as ‘You need to improve this by
giving more detail’

•	 be so detailed that it

o  leads students to the answer, for example you
