you must not give headings or templates that
include examples which give all or part of what
students have to write about or produce.

•

talk the student through how to achieve or
complete the task.

•	 give detail on where to find information/evidence.

In other words, feedback must help the student to take
the initiative in making changes. It must not direct or
tell the student what to do to complete or improve their
work in a way that means they do not need to think
how to apply their learning. Students need to recall or
apply their learning. You must not do the work for the
student(s).

Neither you nor the student can add, amend or remove
any work after the final mark has been submitted for
